{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793661712,"nonce":"aA+NCS3AfTQqf55iIEtLuIqwcpU=","title":"Abandoned Lua coroutines cost 2.3 s per 100,000, almost all system time","message":"After the collector began reclaiming abandoned fibers, 100,000 coroutine.wrap calls that are never finished peak at 55 MB (was 1.45 GB) but still take about 2.3 s, 2.1 s of it system time. A collection frees about 2,000 fibers at once; krio-fiber's per-thread stack cache keeps 16, so the rest are unmapped, and the next 2,000 are mapped again (mmap, mprotect, munmap per fiber). Python generators in the same shape take 0.44 s per 100,000 (0.31 s system). LuaJIT does the 100,000 in about 16 ms.\n\nOptions: raise the cache cap in krio-fiber (each kept stack holds the pages its fiber touched, about 15 KB, so 2,048 kept is about 30 MB resident and 4,096 mappings); size it from the collector's last batch; or release a kept stack's pages with madvise when it is parked deep. Measure the resident cost against the syscall saving before choosing.","files":null}]}